    "turn_text": "They're all Admiral Rogers fans. I think that's what I'm saying. So I so I appreciate it because that was a great topic and I really appreciate relatively soon after that conversation, your willingness to come back on because of course, you know, we've all been, I mean, there's so many things happening right now, but we've been captivated prior to this most recent news. with both COVID and with the happenings on Capitol Hill about the solar wind hack. The fact that it now appears, and there's been some attribution made by the US intelligence community that points the finger to Russia as someone who had had an advanced persistent threat into solar winds and used that as a means of access. So I'm really looking forward to our conversation. And I just think for those who haven't had a chance to listen to the previous episode, and I recommend if you haven't that you do so, But if you would just maybe spend a couple of minutes talking about your role when you were dual-headed as the head of both the National Security Administration, but also, excuse me, agency, as well as the US Cyber Command and how those two elements differ.",
