    "turn_text": "not worked the date, and I don't think it's going to work in the future. You're asking one organization that doesn't have the same luck. Doesn't mean they're not hardworking. It doesn't mean they're not good people. But they are not structured. They're not resourced, and they don't have the expertise. to do it. For example, I would argue it is symptomatic of that in selecting a cyber lead within the National Security Council. Both the Trump administration and the Biden administration selected an NSA individual. Rob Joyce with the Trump team and now Ann Newberger, both NSA individuals in the cybersecurity side. You know, they, again, I think that organization recognizes where deep expertise and deep talent is. But why can't we bring the broader set of capabilities resident with NSA within DOD? I don't understand this idea of, well, we're just going to leave it to Sissa and they're going to do it by themselves. I don't think",
